WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.050
Little Red Riding Hood.

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.050
Let's start the story
a different way.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.220
It was dark inside the wolf.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.100
Human beings are creative
storytelling beings.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.160
They make art because
that's what human beings do.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.550
As a writer, your goal is to
keep your reader believing

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.150
in your story even though
both of you know it's fiction.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.900
When I wrote The
Handmaid's Tale,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.390
nothing went into it that
had not happened in real life

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.500
somewhere at sometime.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.300
The reason I made that rule
is that I didn't want anybody

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.280
saying you certainly
have an evil imagination,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.040
you made up all
these bad things.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.340
I didn't make them up.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.800
If you really do want
to write and you're

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.380
struggling to get started,
you're afraid of something.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.000
Remember, it's only
you and the page.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.370
The waste paper
basket is your friend.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.645
It was invented for you by God.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.800
People are always coming up
with new theories of the novel,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.250
but the main rule is
hold my attention.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.900
Any form of human
creativity is a process

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.270
of doing it and
getting better at it.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.170
You become a writer by writing.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.000
There is no other way.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.600
So do it, do it more.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.800
Do it better.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.540
Fail.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.900
Fail better.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.530
Somewhere out there, there are
the readers for your book.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.690
I'm Margaret Atwood, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.740
[MUSIC PLAYING]

